  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montreal Protocol Multilateral Fund 22-23 Financial Year - Core Contribution - Ozone Layer</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 1991, the Multilateral Fund for the Implementation of the Montreal Protocol (MPMF) has collaborated with partners worldwide to address the depletion of the ozone layer. The mandate of the MPMF is to assist developing country parties to the Montreal Protocol phase out ozone-depleting substances. The Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer is the landmark multilateral environmental agreement that regulates the production and consumption of nearly 100 man-made chemicals referred to as ozone depleting substances. This funding (total value: $10.53 million) represents Australia&apos;s contribution to the MPMF for the 2022-23 Financial Year.</narrative>
  </description>
